                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8ce9c20d-0f5a-4127-a0a6-8dc71f34f763",
                        "entry_id": "c368de86-6eb8-3c63-a75a-f87d0aa0baff",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "блу́дах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e9340774-e3e2-32d0-9d64-1ff6f8f0e6a0",
                        "entry_id": "c368de86-6eb8-3c63-a75a-f87d0aa0baff",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. (половое) распутство, разврат"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4440277a-2231-4c93-b636-a27a96077232",
                                "sense_id": "e9340774-e3e2-32d0-9d64-1ff6f8f0e6a0",
                                "text": "Итак, умертвите земные члены ваши: блуд, нечистоту, страсть, злую похоть и любостяжание, которое есть идолослужение, за которые гнев Божий грядёт на сынов противления, в которых и вы некогда обращались, когда жили между ними."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d42446a5-40b8-498f-8501-03296d80beee",
                                "sense_id": "e9340774-e3e2-32d0-9d64-1ff6f8f0e6a0",
                                "text": "Бегайте блуда; всякий грех, какой делает человек, есть вне тела, а блудник грешит против собственного тела."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ab97205-563a-4e4a-83db-e816ca9e10d8",
                                "sense_id": "e9340774-e3e2-32d0-9d64-1ff6f8f0e6a0",
                                "text": "И дошли мы таким манером до разговора до всякого; рассказал он мне, с чего взялся в человеках и блуд, и воровство, и пьянство, и всякие грехи."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6097fde8-3923-43c0-8c90-693979de0f46",
                                "sense_id": "e9340774-e3e2-32d0-9d64-1ff6f8f0e6a0",
                                "text": "Сектанты крестились двумя перстами, называли троеперстное крестное знамение антихристовой печатью, переменяли себе имена, не возбраняли для вида исповедоваться и причащаться, но брачное сожитие называли блудом, толкуя, что по апокалипсису только девственники войдут «в Царствие Небесное агнца»."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ab8f5a8-1555-4848-a6b7-a0e21b080857",
                                "sense_id": "e9340774-e3e2-32d0-9d64-1ff6f8f0e6a0",
                                "text": "Но ничего не находил царь в обрядах языческих, кроме пьянства, ночных оргий, блуда, кровосмешения и противоестественных страстей, и в догматах их видел суесловие и обман."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c81a521-5216-4d1d-98d5-03773dbb5ed5",
                                "sense_id": "e9340774-e3e2-32d0-9d64-1ff6f8f0e6a0",
                                "text": "— Дед, как ты относишься к сексу? — спросил Серега, вытирая подбородок. — Раньше говорили — блуд. — Как ты относишься к блуду? — Не знаю."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "358059b2-97d9-38e9-b6cf-4fac479f8758",
                        "entry_id": "c368de86-6eb8-3c63-a75a-f87d0aa0baff",
                        "glosses": [
                            "религ. уклонение от прямого, праведного пути, от Божьего промысла"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "56c3664a-d4fc-44cd-a1a8-b5e78231a369",
                                "sense_id": "358059b2-97d9-38e9-b6cf-4fac479f8758",
                                "text": "— Ты не читай книг, — сказал однажды хозяин. — Книга — блуд, блудодейственного ума чадо. Она всего касается, смущает, тревожит."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7788ed07-0279-478a-ad47-9b6403611c9b",
                        "source_entry_id": "c368de86-6eb8-3c63-a75a-f87d0aa0baff",
                        "target_lang_word": "fornication",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fornication",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "706b5425-a2c4-3e8e-a37d-910fc4321f21",
                                        "entry_id": "8e696371-cee9-39e5-993c-09f7d29d8562",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sexual intercourse by people who are not married to each other, or which is considered illicit in another way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a56855a3-db66-4995-bac0-105c2afdc79f",
                                                "sense_id": "706b5425-a2c4-3e8e-a37d-910fc4321f21",
                                                "text": "FRIAR BARNARDINE. Thou hast committed—\nBARABAS. Fornication: but that was in another country;\nAnd besides, the wench is dead."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b68b35a-3838-4a70-ab83-9f0fdb8def0a",
                                                "sense_id": "706b5425-a2c4-3e8e-a37d-910fc4321f21",
                                                "text": "I am the sister of one Claudio,\nCondemned upon the act of fornication\nTo lose his head, condemned by Angelo"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2245ee02-5325-4c18-94f9-805d7c0f8ca1",
                                                "sense_id": "706b5425-a2c4-3e8e-a37d-910fc4321f21",
                                                "text": "Now the works of the flesh are manifest, which are these; Adultery, fornication, uncleanness, lasciviousness, Idolatry, witchcraft, hatred, variance, emulations, wrath, strife, seditions, heresies, Envyings, murders, drunkenness, revellings, and such like: of the which I tell you before, as I have also told you in time past, that they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of God."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8cb6e05-cae0-4f84-99e8-bc651ec88e9c",
                                                "sense_id": "706b5425-a2c4-3e8e-a37d-910fc4321f21",
                                                "text": "Draw not near unto fornication; for it is wickedness, and an evil way"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9ecfca0-8677-45c3-9740-4912e9da4fe4",
                                                "sense_id": "706b5425-a2c4-3e8e-a37d-910fc4321f21",
                                                "text": "In one case, where a man was sued for committing fornication with his wife before marriage, it appeared, that seven years after her death he was cited to stand as a prisoner at their bar, though he had lived with her for nine years,[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af156484-a997-4e9a-b3aa-f0387e06f91b",
                                                "sense_id": "706b5425-a2c4-3e8e-a37d-910fc4321f21",
                                                "text": "... that he was a married man at the time is a necessary allegation, as the allegation that he was an unmarried man would have been necessary had he been charged with the crime of incest, by having committed fornication with his daughter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d38b8d49-88b5-4e5a-a04d-de646ab3e8aa",
                                                "sense_id": "706b5425-a2c4-3e8e-a37d-910fc4321f21",
                                                "text": "Thus, at Roxbury, 1678, Hanna Hopkins was censured in the church for fornication with her husband before marriage and for fleeing from justice into Rhode Island."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f847b36e-449e-373d-b2b7-915020b924d6",
                                        "entry_id": "8e696371-cee9-39e5-993c-09f7d29d8562",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sexual intercourse in general; sex."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23ff6dbd-864f-4af9-a84a-d0d303c74d46",
                                                "sense_id": "f847b36e-449e-373d-b2b7-915020b924d6",
                                                "text": "For a moment he stared at the back of the Lascar, wondering if he were the youth that he had disturbed during fornication with his Engineer, then dismissed all thoughts of the previous night, he was getting old, and suspicious, what did it matter […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "87e339ce-27e7-4992-8bf1-26ad8c86403e",
                        "source_entry_id": "c368de86-6eb8-3c63-a75a-f87d0aa0baff",
                        "target_lang_word": "whoredom",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "whoredom",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38a6422b-e90b-34e9-8a3c-3e62270a155a",
                                        "entry_id": "ddd20209-4f74-30c9-87ee-6310ac51d800",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being a whore, prostitution; sexual indulgence, fornication."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13d1e513-14ec-4daa-8248-f06aef459ecb",
                                                "sense_id": "38a6422b-e90b-34e9-8a3c-3e62270a155a",
                                                "text": "And it came to pass about three months after, that it was told Judah, saying, Tamar thy daughter in law hath played the harlot; and also, behold, she is with child by whoredom. And Judah said, Bring her forth, and let her be burnt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "717d1037-9022-4c7e-a61a-f389408f0f5e",
                                                "sense_id": "38a6422b-e90b-34e9-8a3c-3e62270a155a",
                                                "text": "Mother[…]considered that the exclusiveness of Peter's circle was due not to its distinction, but to the fact that it was an inner Babylon of prodigality and whoredom, from which every Kensingtonian held aloof, except on the conventional tip-and-run excursions in pursuit of shopping, tea and theatres."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71ef2bba-0ccf-49c7-b01c-9733ed8ebb18",
                                                "sense_id": "38a6422b-e90b-34e9-8a3c-3e62270a155a",
                                                "text": "Force not your slave-girls to whoredom that ye may seek enjoyment of the life of the world, if they would preserve their chastity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ff94399-7d5c-4506-b0b0-293a573abc9b",
                                                "sense_id": "38a6422b-e90b-34e9-8a3c-3e62270a155a",
                                                "text": "the most enthusiastic punishers of whoredom were often the most evangelical Protestants, who sought the ever-further purification of society (‘Puritans’, as they came to be called in England)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "93e43f7d-fa83-48ce-98b7-d998fa9293bb",
